2. **P1 — Exposure and frontend isolation: FIXED.**  
   R2:10,43 removes importer-based authorization and states installation-family exposure. Source agrees: `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1289–1307` inherits linked entries into installation children; `:1396–1403` retains admission records and transfers child dependencies; `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:552–554` resolves registry hits before issuing requests. Frontend runtime isolation is correctly outside this design.

   “Untrust is not retroactive” now means policy changes affect unanswered questions, without eviction, response revocation, or reversal of an existing allow. This agrees with first-answer retention in `src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc:95–108`.

3. **P1 — Tick-to-VM handoff: FIXED architecturally.**  
   R2:47–54 chooses a concrete handoff: retain the round successor, pass initial progress through the pending driver, run the VM once without another interpreter round, then continue the bounded loop.

   This addresses the source gap: `src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:554–579` advances the request cursor when delivering a response, whereas `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1398–1407` runs the VM only when its own iteration reports progress. Passing the tick’s progress prevents that delivered response from being stranded.

   The proposed `::linker` carry preserves the consolidation of state currently carried by `link-raise`/`carry-served` at `repl.cljc:1253–1289`, including rollback through `:1956–1996`. The mutually exclusive progress/event branches avoid two rechecks for one tick. Acceptance (a) and (b) catch the lost-progress regression; (c) catches successor loss on refusal; (d) catches idle rechecks. Additional precision is suggested below.

4. **P1 — AL-1 boundary versus acceptance: FIXED.**  
   R2:85 preserves every public var, `composition`/`serve`, and session topology. API reduction and dht-only admission-pair minting move to AL-2. This matches current construction at `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:773–793` and the public definitions in both relocated namespaces.

