   The sentence says “the drain's cursor and the serial move even in a round that reports none.” In `src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc`, `drain` never changes `:serial`; `ask` increments it only after successfully appending a question. Section 7.5.6 expressly counts that append as progress. The serial therefore cannot advance in a no-progress round under the specified behavior.  
